  "body": "The `site` job of `release.yml` run 45269109413 (tag v0.26.0, commit fe385c642) failed at the step \"Site tests\". Thus the `pages` job did not deploy the site. A user cannot see the 0.26.0 documentation on https://neotech.github.io/Camcraft/.\n\nThis is the same drift as #3271. `main` at 4e7929dfe fails the same 6 tests (local run with zola 0.23.6, `PYTHONUTF8=1`).\n\nFailures:\n\n1. `test_guide_icons.py:105` and `:113`: `site/static/icons/op-multiaxis-deburr.png` and `site/static/icons/op-waterjet-profile.png` are missing. The app icons exist in `assets/ui/`.\n2. `test_operation_reference.py:59`: the operation reference has no section for `WaterjetProfile` and `MultiAxisDeburr`.\n3. `test_post_processor_reference.py:32`: the post-processor reference has no entry for the engine hooks `onJetOn` and `onJetOff`.\n4. `test_post_processor_reference.py:23`: the post-processor reference has no rows for the manifest properties `lineEnding`, `linearizeArcs` and `uprightReturn`.\n\nCause: the features of 0.26.0 merged without their site pages. Nothing runs `site/tests` before a cut (see the P5 follow-up).\n\nDone means:\n- `python3 -m unittest discover -s site/tests` passes on `main`.\n- A branch `site/v0.26.0` from the tag has the same site-only fix, and a `site_only` dispatch of `release.yml` deploys \"CamCraft 0.26.0\" with the app at `/app/`.\n",
